    "pressure": {
      "file": "dry_scrubber_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Acid gas falls as sorbent reacts",
      "description": "Fine dry sorbent injected into the hot flue gas reacts with acid gases: Ca(OH)₂ + SO₂ → CaSO₃ + H₂O, Ca(OH)₂ + 2 HCl → CaCl₂ + 2 H₂O (or sodium bicarbonate, which decomposes to very reactive Na₂CO₃ above ≈ 140 °C). Removal depends on temperature, residence time, mixing and the stoichiometric ratio (often 1.5–3); the fabric filter cake adds further contact. No liquid effluent — the product is a dry powder; recirculation improves sorbent use.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
